[36m(TaskRunner pid=1617240)[0m You are now at step 22 and your current observation is: sender='user' message="Oh, 128GB! Great, that's the one I wanted. Thank you for checking on that for me. That puts my mind at ease knowing I at least got that right.\n\nSo let me recap - the order for my daughter was cancelled, and it was going to my address here in Denver instead of hers in Chicago, which explains why she never got it. There's no tracking number since it's cancelled, and I'll need to reorder those things for her. And the tablet is 128GB, which is correct. Did I get all that right?\n\nAs for changing the default address, I'll have to call my daughter to get her exact address and then call back. Would I be able to get through to someone like you again, or would I just call the regular customer service number?\n\nI want to thank you for being so patient with me today. I know I wasn't the most prepared caller you've ever had. It's just... well, it's nice having someone to talk to, even if it's just about orders and shipping addresses. You've been real kind, and I appreciate that more than you know. \n\nIs there anything else you need from me, or should I let you get back to your other calls? I'm sure there are plenty of other folks out there needing your help. Though I can't imagine any of them being as scattered as I've been today, haha."
