[36m(TaskRunner pid=1764613)[0m     "snippet": "---\ntitle: 25 Age Gaps Between Actors Who Played Parent And Child That Are So Small, It's Blowing My Mind\ndate: 2024-11-30\n---\n25 Age Gaps Between Actors Who Played Parent And Child That Are So Small, It's Blowing My Mind\n\nWe asked the members of the BuzzFeed Community to tell us what age gap between actors who played parent and child surprised them. Here are some of their eye-opening answers:\n\n1.Tom Holland was 25 when he starred in The Crowded Room.\n\nEmmy Rossum was 35 when she starred in the show.\n\nIn the series, she played his mother, despite only being 10 years older.\n\n2.Elvis Presley was 26 when he filmed Blue Hawaii.\n\nAngela Lansbury was 35 when she filmed the movie.\n\nAngela played his mother in the film, despite only being nine years older.\n\n3.Michael J. Fox was 23 when he starred in Back to the Future.\n\nCrispin Glover was 20 years old in the film.\n\nIn the film, Cripsin plays the father of Michael's character in both the past and present, despite being three years YOUNGER than Michael.\n\n4.Kate Mara was 25 during the filming of Brokeback Mountain.\n\nHeath Ledger was 25 during filming.\n\nIn the movie, they played father and daughter, despite Heath only being four years older.\n\n5.Adam Garcia was 28 when Riding in Cars with Boys came out.\n\nDrew Barrymore was 26 when the film came out.\n\nSo Adam Garcia was two years older than Drew Barrymore when he played her son in the film.\n\n6.Elizabeth Rodriguez was born in 1980.\n\nDascha Polanco was born in 1982.\n\nIn Orange Is the New Black, Elizabeth Rodriguez played Dascha Polanco's mother even though they have a two-year age gap.\n\n7.Gina Rodriguez was 29 when Jane the Virgin started filming.\n\nAndrea Navedo was 36 when it started filming.\n\nIn Jane the Virgin, Andrea Navedo and Gina Rodriguez played mother and daughter, despite having only a seven-year age gap.\n\n8.Taron Egerton was 28 when Rocketman, started filming.\n\nBryce Dallas Howard was 37 during filming.\n\nThey played mother and son in the film, despite only having a nine-year age gap.\n\n9.Rachel McAd"
