[36m(TaskRunner pid=1764613)[0m     "snippet": "---\ntitle: 30 Age Gaps Between Actors Who Played Parent And Child That Make No Sense In Real Life\nauthor: Ilona Bali\u016bnait\u0117\ndate: 2021-01-27\n---\n30 Age Gaps Between Actors Who Played Parent And Child That Make No Sense In Real Life\n\nWhile it's certainly naive to think that everything we see in the movies is real, some of the lies they pull off are really impressive. Like the actual age gaps between some of the actors who play parent and child. Take Heath Ledger and Kate Mara in Brokeback Mountain, for example. At the time of producing the movie, Ledger was 25 and Mara was 21. Yet their portrayal of Ennis and Alma Jr. was totally believable!\n\nAnd this isn't a one-time thing; it happens more than you're probably aware of. But don't worry, Bored Panda is here to open your eyes. We have compiled a list of on-screen relatives with ridiculous real-life age differences, so sit back, continue scrolling, and you'll have a better understanding of Hollywood in no time.\n\nThis post may include affiliate links.\n\nEstelle Getty Was Actually Younger Than Bea Arthur When She Played Her Mom In Golden Girls\n\nBut wait, there's more awkwardness when it comes to co-stars playing each other's relatives. For instance, they may end up having to work with people who have dated their exes. Weird, right? But I've got something even spicier. How about portraying family members with someone you actually date in real life!\n\nIt may sound unnatural to us but these are top-class professionals we're talking about and they have no problem with it. Georgia Moffett and David Tennant were daughter and father in Dr. Who but they started dating and even got married in 2011!\n\nAlso, Chris Pratt dated Emily VanCamp.These two secretly got together when they started to work together on Everwood, playing brother and sister but broke up after a couple of years together.\n\nAngelina Jolie Was Colin Farrell's Mom In Alexander, But In Reality They're Only A Year Apart\n\nThere's also a really meta example of these types of interesting relationship dynamics. Arrested Development was a show that had numerous references to incest and one time, the showrunners actually used a brother and sister duo to portray potential lovers.\n\nIn the episode \"Family Ties\", Michael Bluth (played by Jason Bateman) believes that he has another sister named N"
